# nocheck: persona-block-rationale - OpenBao's UI login is not a link-then-Keycloak journey the shared persona helper can drive: the Ember auth form requires selecting the OIDC method, resolving the role through POST /v1/auth/oidc/oidc/auth_url, then completing Keycloak in a popup that posts its result back via postMessage (see upstream ui/app/components/auth-jwt.js). The administrator's full OIDC journey is asserted by the role-local files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js instead; with SSO off the administrator signs in through the same Ember auth form with the LDAP method or, without a directory, the userpass method, which files/playwright/test-design.js drives.
PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true

# nocheck: persona-block-rationale - biber holds no OpenBao RBAC group, so by design it receives only the `default` policy and reaches no authenticated OpenBao surface; that denial is asserted by test-rbac-denial.js instead of a persona journey.
PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true

